# Scratch working directories used by the CuTe reduction work: run logs, gate
# harnesses, probe corpora and measurement evidence.  They are the audit trail behind
# the numbers in these PRs and are kept on disk, but they are not library code and are
# deliberately NOT tracked -- ~1500 files / 43 MB of them.
#
# ⚠ Listing them here is what keeps ``git status`` clean for anyone who has such a
# directory locally.  Without these entries the working tree shows them as untracked,
# and the pressure to make ``git status`` quiet is what got them committed once before
# (along with a ``pyproject.toml`` hunk adding Ruff per-file exemptions for exactly
# these paths, which is the tell that scratch was being treated as shippable).
_notes/
_notes2/
_notes_overnight/
_notes_codereview/
_notes_codereview2/
_redfix/
_redfix2/
_redfix3/
